  "runner_up_case": "The strongest honest case for FALSE rests on three gaps rather than any affirmative counter-evidence. (1) Court attribution is thin: of the contemporaneous sources, only CoStar (2025-10-17) names the Innsbruck Regional Court; The Local (2025-10-15) says only 'an Austrian court' and Wikipedia only 'in Austria'. The decisive detail in the claim therefore hangs on a single secondary outlet. (2) No primary or official confirmation exists in the file: the only docket check run was court_records, which indexes US courts and is structurally incapable of confirming an Austrian Landesgericht judgment — its empty result proves nothing, but it also means no court press release, docket, or Austrian-language reporting (ORF, APA) was ever obtained. (3) Sentence precision and finality: 'two years' is taken from headlines and snippets; Austrian first-instance fraud verdicts are frequently partially suspended and subject to appeal, and the team's own later evidence shows the picture moved on — the OGH overturned part of the Innsbruck outcome and a September 2026 retrial produced 30 months — so the October 2025 pronouncement was not final and its terms were subsequently revised. If the October 2025 hearing was in fact a trial opening, remand, or adjournment misread as a verdict, or if the pronounced sentence differed from a flat two years, or if the court was not the Innsbruck Regional Court, the claim as stated is materially wrong. That said, this is an uphill case: three independent outlets dated 15–17 October 2025 agree on a two-year sentence, and the September 2026 coverage back-references it as historical fact, so FALSE requires a specific findable error, not mere doubt.",
  "would_flip_it": [
    "An official Landesgericht Innsbruck press release, docket entry, or authoritative Austrian reporting (ORF/APA) showing that no conviction or sentence was pronounced on or around 15 October 2025 — e.g., that the hearing was a trial opening, remand decision, or adjournment misreported as a verdict.",
    "A published correction or retraction from The Local, its underlying agency (AFP), or CoStar withdrawing the 15–17 October 2025 reports of a two-year prison sentence.",
    "An authoritative source showing the October 2025 pronouncement differed materially from the claim — a different sentence length, a fully suspended or conditional sentence, or judgment by a court other than the Innsbruck Regional Court (which only CoStar names).",
    "Evidence that the October 2025 Innsbruck proceedings concerned a different René Benko (a namesake) rather than the Signa founder, or that the 'two years' figure belongs solely to the September 2026 retrial with the October 2025 reports having described a different outcome."
  ]
}
